Subject: Remove the switches that are always off

What this does
  Drops `QJS_REGVM_INLOOP_CALL` and `JS_MEGA_DISABLE` and their branches,
  keeping the off path. The `INLOOP_CALL || RECORD` guards become
  `QJS_REGVM_RECORD`; the bare `INLOOP_CALL` blocks (the nested-frame
  interpreter) are deleted. `JS_MEGA_DISABLE`'s `#if !JS_MEGA_DISABLE` guards
  are unwrapped, so the megamorphic stub cache is always compiled in.
  `REGVM_SLIM_FRAME`, which was derived as `RECORD && !INLOOP_CALL`, becomes
  `QJS_REGVM_RECORD`.

Why we need it
  Nothing sets either switch, and neither non-default setting compiles, so
  both off branches are dead. The switches and their source only obscure the
  one configuration that exists.

What it adds
  No new API. Runtime only.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

